WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.050
Not all heroes wear capes.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.009
Some of them wear Pokemon t-shirts and a baseball
cap.

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:10.870
You might think you’ve heard of every superhero
out there, with Marvel and DC dominating the

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:16.750
box office, and the incredible Cactus Man
fighting crime on the mean streets of Edinburgh,

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.970
but there is one tiny aspiring hero you’ve
likely never heard of.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:27.000
In a world filled with danger and evildoers,
one young boy armed with a pure heart and

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.599
some telekinetic powers dared to step up and
save the day.

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:36.980
A woman was being abducted at gunpoint when
seven-year-old Cameron spotted the struggle.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.320
He saw the weapon in the man’s hand, the
fear in the woman’s eyes as she looked for

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.960
a way out, and he knew that he had to act.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.550
He concentrated with all his might, reaching
out with his mind, and threw the gun out of

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.900
the man’s grasp and into some nearby bushes.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.790
The woman ran as fast as she could from there,
but not before catching a glimpse of the child

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.510
that had saved her life.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:03.910
Somehow, she knew that he had been her hero.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.280
Unfortunately for Cameron, but fortunately
for the SCP Foundation, the woman reported

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.789
what had happened to a nearby police officer,
who just so happened to be an undercover agent

00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:15.320
for the Foundation.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:20.159
Before Cameron could leave the scene, he was
being approached by a team of armed guards,

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:25.079
and brought to a strange new place filled
with men in lab coats, who kept calling him

00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:28.130
“SCP-2241.”

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:33.030
Cameron sat for a very long time in a white
room, wondering whether he was in trouble,

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.570
when a new man in a lab coat entered.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:40.939
He introduced himself as Researcher Valdez
and told Cameron he was going to ask him some

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:41.939
questions.

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:46.299
He asked why Cameron had helped the woman,
instead of running away and getting an adult

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:47.299
to help.

00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:49.869
He said, “Superheroes have to help people!

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:53.890
I can move things without touching them and
other people can't so I should use that to

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:54.890
help them!”

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:59.320
He went on to explain that he had practiced
his ability in the woods, and kept it a secret

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.380
from everyone.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:05.039
Valdez asked what sort of things Cameron could
do, and he explained: “I can move stuff

00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:08.709
without touching it, but not if it's too far
away or if it's too big.

00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:12.030
Only like a cup across a room or a person's
arm or something.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.540
Sometimes it can sorta change as well.”

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.340
When prompted, he elaborated, “Sometimes
when I'm moving something it changes to something

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.340
I want.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.610
Like one time when I was moving a stone, it
changed to look like a toy I lost.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.340
But it changed back after a while, before
I even got home.”

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.760
Cameron became distressed during the interview,
but Valdez promised him that he would be okay

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.760
here.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.470
He asked Cameron what his superhero name would
be, and he told him: Cameron the Crusader.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.040
Valdez explained that Cameron would be staying
at the SCP Foundation for a while, so they

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:47.980
could learn more about his powers, and help
him become a better superhero.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:53.540
Researcher Valdez concluded his interview
with this closing statement: “SCP-2241 appears

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.890
to trust me and believes that the Foundation
is attempting to help him as much as possible.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:04.260
SCP-2241's account is consistent with the
early stages of a humanoid developing a reality-bending

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.590
ability.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:11.299
SCP-2241 may have experienced abuse at the
hands of its parents, leading to early development

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:12.680
of said ability.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.950
In the event that a more developed ability
is required for research, similar emotional

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.050
stress can be applied by Foundation staff.”

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.569
SCP-2241 is kept in a standard humanoid containment
chamber.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:28.709
He is given access to television and comic
books, though this access can be cut off as

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:30.250
punishment for bad behavior.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:35.269
He is fed three balanced meals a day, with
additional treats such as chocolate or ice

00:03:35.269 --> 00:03:40.250
cream provided after testing, especially if
the testing goes on for a particularly long

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.069
time or is exceptionally stressful.

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:48.630
All personnel that interact with SCP-2241
are to call him by his name, Cameron, when

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.359
interacting with him.

00:03:50.359 --> 00:03:54.920
Only Cameron’s assigned psychologist and
specifically designated personnel, such as

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.769
Valdez are allowed to develop a friendly relationship
with him.

00:03:58.769 --> 00:04:03.620
If he becomes attached to an unapproved person,
they are required to discourage this however

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:04.950
they can.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:09.629
After containment procedures were established,
Valdez and his team set to work putting together

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:14.470
tests that would use Cameron’s emotions
and desire to save people in order to develop

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.160
and strengthen his abilities.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.910
For the first test, they deliberately exposed
Cameron to a D-Class that believed him to

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:25.680
be a valuable hostage, one that he could use
to escape from the Foundation.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.100
The D-Class abducted Cameron at knife-point,
but Cameron quickly used his reality-bending

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.440
ability to turn the knife into chocolate and
escape.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:39.080
The knife remained chocolate and did not turn
back to metal, indicating his powers had grown

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.080
stronger.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:44.319
Details of events that followed this test
have been redacted from the official file,

00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:48.979
but a note from a member of the Overwatch
Council provides a peek into what might have

00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:54.530
happened: “SCP-2241 has stated that it intends
to grow stronger to stop more people from

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.330
dying, and this will help both it and us in
this aim.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:03.660
Killing a man with a teleported bullet was
a stroke of tactical genius from the SCP object.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:09.280
MTF-Theta-17 will be ready to respond during
all further rounds of testing as a precaution.”

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.020
Following a series of tests, each of which
included heightened emotional stakes such

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:20.210
as threatening the lives of innocent bystanders
or treasured items belonging to SCP-2241,

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.830
his abilities developed even further.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:27.979
In one test, a series of armed drones were
made to artificially malfunction, posing an

00:05:27.979 --> 00:05:31.150
apparent threat to Foundation personnel around
the boy.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:36.300
He responded by using his telekinesis to turn
the drones on each other, crashing them into

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.300
one another.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:42.319
When only one drone remained, he teleported
its weaponry to a nearby field, leaving a

00:05:42.319 --> 00:05:44.370
harmless shell behind.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.580
In another test, a bomb was detonated near
a member of D-class personnel.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:53.729
The boy somehow absorbed the energy of the
bomb as it exploded, transforming its kinetic

00:05:53.729 --> 00:05:57.020
energy and saving the man’s life.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:01.080
Another bomb-related test featured a man with
a bomb strapped to him attacking a D-class.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.270
In this test, it was ordered that the bomber
be taken alive.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:10.330
Cameron responded by teleporting the bomb
vest into an explosion-proof containment chamber,

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:14.900
and knocking the bomber unconscious with a
single punch, though his tiny fist should

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:18.479
not have been capable of delivering such a
strong blow.

00:06:18.479 --> 00:06:25.440
In another test, a third bomb was placed in
SCP-2241’s chamber among his personal belongings,

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.830
including some stuffed animals and comic books.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:32.870
He was very upset at this discovery, and teleported
the bomb high up into the sky where it detonated

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:33.870
harmlessly.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.270
He remained upset for a while after, repeating,
“no one can take my things.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:38.270
It's not fair.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:39.379
I'm strong.

00:06:39.379 --> 00:06:40.560
I'm the crusader.”

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.199
Moving on from bombs, the Research Team tasked
the boy with stealing a box from a Foundation

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:48.729
bank vault, which had been modified for extra
security.

00:06:48.729 --> 00:06:53.420
He teleported himself into the vault, picked
up the box, and then made a mistake: he tripped

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:54.759
the sensors inside.

00:06:54.759 --> 00:06:59.389
However, he somehow slowed the sensors down
and was able to teleport himself back out

00:06:59.389 --> 00:07:02.039
of the vault before the alarm could sound.

00:07:02.039 --> 00:07:07.129
This was the first task given to Cameron that
could be perceived as morally grey, or even

00:07:07.129 --> 00:07:13.020
villainous, but he performed it without question,
and this was recorded as a notable development.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:17.569
Next, a surprise long-range attack was performed
on the Foundation Site by a Foundation-owned

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:23.550
robotic mortar. 2241 became angry, catching
the bomb and throwing it toward the launcher

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:28.139
at a speed that appeared to be approximately
1.4 times the speed of sound.

00:07:28.139 --> 00:07:32.241
It was noted that his abilities were less
focused, and his demeanor more violent, when

00:07:32.241 --> 00:07:33.320
he was angry.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.650
He turned to an observing researcher and said,
“I hate them.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:40.080
I’m a Foundation Avenger and I hate the
bad guys and I’m gonna fight them all.”

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:46.260
For the final test in this series, two D-Classes,
who were described to 2411 as civilians, were

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.580
held at gunpoint in rooms with bulletproof
glass windows.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:54.379
He was told that the guns could not be affected
by his powers, the hostages needed physical

00:07:54.379 --> 00:07:59.330
contact to be teleported to safety, and he
needed to rescue them both before they were

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.330
killed.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:05.130
Shocking the research team, he split into
two versions of himself, each teleporting

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:10.000
a hostage to safety before returning to the
crime scene to subdue the “bad guys.”

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.960
He reported feeling a bit sick afterwards,
but had no other adverse effects from splitting

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.500
himself into two people.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:21.780
By the time this series of tests was completed,
he was able to teleport objects as well as

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:27.930
his own body, duplicate himself, see a few
seconds into the future, and move or transform

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:30.879
objects within a distance of twelve meters.

00:08:30.879 --> 00:08:35.860
He was excited about these improvements, referring
to them as “leveling up.”

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:41.950
Following these tests, Valdez planned to pause
the psychiatric treatment of SCP-2241 in favor

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.550
of a more hands-on approach.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:48.860
The plan was to begin neurological testing
using a surgically implanted chip that would

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:51.730
monitor the boy’s brain activity during
combat.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.630
The Ethics Committee caught wind of this and
immediately intervened.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:59.980
They temporarily revoked Valdez’s security
clearance and placed him under investigation.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:04.579
They submitted an official report on this
decision, which read: “Implanting a monitoring

00:09:04.579 --> 00:09:08.920
chip into a child this young can not be done
without significant developmental damage in

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.190
later years.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:14.350
This will cause catastrophic problems for
both the child and long term containment,

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.570
given his well developed capabilities.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:21.480
Additionally, deploying a child in combat,
even under testing conditions, violates all

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.279
moral norms.

00:09:23.279 --> 00:09:27.800
Personnel involved in sweeping the previous
rapid-fire tests under the rug are under review.”

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:33.130
The testing and research surrounding SCP-2241
did not only draw the attention of the Ethics

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:38.190
Committee, but it also caused discord within
the Overwatch Council itself.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:42.800
Following the Ethics Committee intervention,
O5-3 ordered that the testing be resumed,

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:47.410
writing: “These tests are more important
than one SCP, regardless of whether it looks

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:48.730
like a child.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:53.680
Long-term containment and observation is no
longer a priority, given the utility of data

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.640
we have collected via intensive testing in
the short term.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:01.640
The risk of the SCP breaching containment
is minimal, given its loyalty.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:06.269
We now know which parts of the brain deal
with certain anomalous abilities.

00:10:06.269 --> 00:10:08.790
With more detail, we can see how.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:14.480
We may even learn how to induce these abilities
- and we will definitely learn how to neutralize

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.480
them.”

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:19.410
Two other members of the Council were horrified
by this statement, believing that it went

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.500
against decency and morality in a way that
could not be justified.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:26.880
O5-4 submitted a statement: “This is too
far.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.490
We can not let this stand as precedent.

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:34.639
This is but one step removed from child soldiers
and even less removed from militarizing an

00:10:34.639 --> 00:10:35.970
SCP-level object.”

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:41.050
An emergency Council meeting was called to
address this internal disagreement, and the

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:47.040
majority voted in favor of reinstating testing,
and exonerating Valdez of all ethics violations.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.560
“I believe the results will justify both
the risks and the means.

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:55.260
We are closer than ever to understanding the
mechanism by which human brains interact with

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:57.050
extranormal phenomena.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:03.420
The emotional and eventual neurological damage
to SCP-2241 is… unfortunate but it is also

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:06.120
necessary for the advancement of our understanding.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:11.800
In addition, due to the new modification of
the monitoring hardware, 2241 can be neutralized

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.660
quickly should it become a threat at any time
after the surgery.”

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:20.089
And so, the protests of the Ethics Committee
were ignored, the concerned members of the

00:11:20.089 --> 00:11:25.990
Overwatch Council overruled, and Valdez was
allowed to resume his plan for testing and

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:30.180
preparing to craft a superpowered child into
a weapon.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:36.920
And all the while, a little boy named Cameron
remained the test subject of the SCP Foundation,

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:42.680
still dreaming of the day when he might have
a chance to save the world.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:49.399
Now go check out “SCP-953 - Polymorphic
Humanoid” and “SCP-213 - Anti-Matter Parasite”

00:11:49.399 --> 00:11:51.790
for more superpowered humanoid anomalies!

